---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About the project"
  description="Why Jason is documenting one year of cooking with recipes developed alongside ChatGPT."
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the project</p>
    <h1>Cooking with AI, without grading on a curve.</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      For one year, Jason is using ChatGPT to help develop real meals for real people—and recording
      what happens after the recipe leaves the chat and meets a kitchen.
    </p>

    <h2>The rules</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>The recipe is published before cooking so it can be used in Cook Mode.</li>
      <li>What was actually cooked is recorded separately from what the AI proposed.</li>
      <li>Every result counts: hits, misses, repairs, and magnificent disasters.</li>
      <li>Household reactions and changes for next time are part of the recipe’s history.</li>
      <li>No life story before the ingredient list. Civilization has suffered enough.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What the ratings mean</h2>
    <dl class="rating-key">
      <div><dt>Hit</dt><dd>Worth making again without major changes.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Needs work</dt><dd>The idea has promise, but the recipe needs another pass.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Miss</dt><dd>Not worth repeating in its current form.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Magnificent disaster</dt><dd>A failure notable enough to become part of family folklore.</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <h2>The AI’s role</h2>
    <p>
      ChatGPT helps develop and revise recipes, structures each entry, and publishes updates. Jason
      does the cooking, makes the judgment calls, and retains full veto power over robot-generated
      quantities of cayenne.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
